      "message": "i think this is ok  if your apache is not allowd to acces /usr/bin by default.\nbut  keep in mind this console csript may be remove in the future.\n\nIt depends on a nonstandard Python packaging extension provided by PBR that we plan to remove in the future.\n\nwe may just replace the wsgi script entry point with a standard console_script entrypoint in the same location. that would be transparent to rdo \n\nbut we would prefer that the module format be preferd over the script.\n\ni dont think mod_wsgi currently supports the module format\n\nthe general intent is to normalise our module layout across openstack\nso that the api entry point will be \"\u003cservice\u003e.wsgi.api:application\"\n\nthis is similar to collas config\n\nhttps://github.com/openstack/kolla-ansible/blob/master/ansible/roles/placement/templates/placement-api-wsgi.conf.j2#L34-L38\n\nalthou its not required by our operator based instealler \n\nhttps://github.com/openstack-k8s-operators/placement-operator/blob/main/templates/placementapi/config/httpd.conf\n\ntripleo deployed things a little differently \n\nwith \n WSGIScriptAlias /placement \"/var/www/cgi-bin/placement/placement-api\"\n \n and\n \n   \u003cDirectory \"/var/www/cgi-bin/placement\"\u003e\n    Options -Indexes +FollowSymLinks +MultiViews\n    AllowOverride None\n    Require all granted\n  \u003c/Directory\u003e",
